## Configuration Template (my.cnf)

```ini
[mysqld]
basedir = /mnt/mtwo/programming/ai-stuff/games/wow-chat-2/mysql/installed-files
datadir = /mnt/mtwo/programming/ai-stuff/games/wow-chat-2/mysql/databases
socket  = /mnt/mtwo/programming/ai-stuff/games/wow-chat-2/mysql/databases/mysql.sock
port    = 3307  # Different port to avoid conflicts

[client]
socket  = /mnt/mtwo/programming/ai-stuff/games/wow-chat-2/mysql/databases/mysql.sock
port    = 3307
```

## Git Tracking Strategy

Database files will be tracked in git so custom world modifications are preserved.
This includes:
- Custom NPC entries
- Modified loot tables
- Quest adjustments
- Spell tweaks for balance

Large binary files (ibdata1, ib_logfile*) may need git-lfs if they grow too large.

Runtime files (*.pid, *.sock, binlog.*) are gitignored.

